                                                "sense_id": "1459a39c-b05d-3187-b6a9-1176f511c54c",
                                                "text": "Trip-hop, on the other hand, takes the opposite approach. The genre can be described as a slower and dub-influenced reworking of African American hip-hop, aptly described by writer Phil Johnson as “dubbed-up hip-hop derived music...beats whose customary urgency is deconstructed into dreamy, erotic soundscapes.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
